      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x = 9\\), we first rewrite it in standard form:\n\\[x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0.\\]\nLet \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) be the roots of this polynomial. By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships among the roots:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9.\n\\]\nWe need to find the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). To do this, we express each term in the sum in a more manageable form:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot sr + st \\cdot sr + tr \\cdot sr}{rst} = \\frac{r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2}{rst}.\n\\]\nSubstituting the value of \\(rst\\) from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2}{9}.\n\\]\nWe can rewrite the numerator \\(r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2\\) using the identity:\n\\[\nr^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t).\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\(rs + rt + st\\) and \\(rst\\), we have:\n\\[\nr^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54.\n\\]\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{-54}{9} = -6.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) is \\(\\boxed{-6}\\).",
