      "text": "To solve the problem \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) given that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are solutions to the equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x = 9\\), we need to first find the roots of the polynomial equation.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0 \\]\n\nLet the roots be \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\). By Vieta's formulas:\n- The sum of the roots \\( r + s + t = 5 \\)\n- The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\( rs + rt + st = 6 \\)\n- The product of the roots \\( rst = 9 \\)\n\nWe need to find:\n\\[ \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} \\]\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression in terms of the roots:\n\\[ \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} \\]\n\nWe can factor this expression by finding a common denominator:\n\\[ \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot tr + tr \\cdot st}{rst} \\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\\[ rs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot tr + tr \\cdot st = (rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2 \\]\n\nNext, we use the identity:\n\\[ (rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2 = (rs + st + tr)^2 - 2rst(s + t + r) \\]\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\\[ rs + st + tr = 6 \\]\n\\[ rst = 9 \\]\n\\[ s + t + r = 5 \\]\n\nNow, calculate:\n\\[ (rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 \\]\n\\[ = 36 - 90 \\]\n\\[ = -54 \\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{(rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2}{rst} = \\frac{-54}{9} \\]\n\\[ = -6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}\n\\]",
