      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start by using Vieta's formulas for the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\). According to Vieta's formulas, for a cubic equation of the form \\(x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), the relationships between the roots \\(r, s, t\\) and the coefficients are:\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = -a\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = b\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = -c\n\\]\n\nFor the equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\), we identify the coefficients as follows:\n\\[\na = -5, \\quad b = 6, \\quad c = -9\n\\]\n\nUsing these coefficients, we can determine the sums and products of the roots:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the expression \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). To do this, we first express each term in terms of \\(r, s, t\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs \\cdot st}{t \\cdot st} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{rst} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{9}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{st}{r} = \\frac{st \\cdot rt}{r \\cdot rt} = \\frac{s^2 t^2}{rst} = \\frac{s^2 t^2}{9}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{tr \\cdot rs}{s \\cdot rs} = \\frac{t^2 r^2}{rst} = \\frac{t^2 r^2}{9}\n\\]\n\nAdding these terms together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{9} + \\frac{s^2 t^2}{9} + \\frac{t^2 r^2}{9} = \\frac{r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2}{9}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value of \\(r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2\\). We can use the identity:\n\n\\[\n(r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2) = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\), \\(rst = 9\\), and \\(r + s + t = 5\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nr^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2}{9} = \\frac{-54}{9} = -6\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}\n\\]",
