      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\), we know that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of this equation. By Vieta's formulas, we have the following relationships among the roots:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9.\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the expression \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). We can rewrite this expression in terms of the roots \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs \\cdot rs}{rst \\cdot rst \\cdot rst} = \\frac{r^2 s^2 t^2}{rst \\cdot rst \\cdot rst} = \\frac{(rst)^2}{(rst)^2} = \\frac{(rst)^2}{(rst)^2} = \\frac{(rst)^2}{(rst)^2} = \\frac{(rst)^2}{(rst)^2} = \\frac{(rst)^2}{(rst)^2}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the value of \\(rst = 9\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{9^2}{9^2} = \\frac{81}{81} = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
